# 5. THREE PERMANENT USER MODES
==================================================

EFBTOUR must have exactly three primary user roles:

1. OWNER MODE.
2. MANAGEMENT MODE.
3. PLAYER MODE.

Each account must have one primary role.

During account setup, display three professional role-selection cards.

### OWNER MODE

For users who want to own and manage their own teams.

### MANAGEMENT MODE

For authorized tournament management personnel.

### PLAYER MODE

For users who participate as individual eFootball players.

## ROLE LOCK SYSTEM

- One account can select only one primary role.
- Once selected, the role is permanently locked to that account.
- No role-switching option.
- No role-switching button in Settings.
- Logout cannot reset the role.
- Reinstalling the app cannot reset the role.
- Changing devices cannot reset the role.

Management Mode must be provisioned or approved by Super Admin to prevent unauthorized administrative access.

Owner and Player registrations can follow the public registration process.

## ACCOUNT DELETION RULE

Role locking applies to an account, not permanently to a person.

If an account is permanently deleted, the user can register a new account and select a new role.

Historical tournament records must be preserved appropriately.

Deletion must follow a secure account-deletion workflow.

