## AUCTION RULES

1. Only authorized Team Owners can place bids.
2. Only eligible registered players can enter the auction.
3. Highest valid bid wins.
4. Purchased players are automatically assigned to the winning team.
5. Deduct the winning bid from the team's virtual budget.
6. One player cannot be purchased by two teams in the same tournament.
7. A team cannot exceed 10 active player positions.
8. Management controls auction opening and closing.
9. Maintain complete auction history.
10. Prevent duplicate and invalid bids.
11. Prevent spending beyond available virtual budget.
12. Handle simultaneous bids using backend transactions.

Use tournament-specific virtual auction credits.

Do not introduce real-money payment functionality unless separately authorized and properly implemented.

==================================================
# 12. TEAM VS TEAM MATCH SCORING SYSTEM
==================================================

Each BID Tournament team has exactly 10 active players.

When Team A plays Team B:

A1 vs B1.
A2 vs B2.
A3 vs B3.
A4 vs B4.
A5 vs B5.
A6 vs B6.
A7 vs B7.
A8 vs B8.
A9 vs B9.
A10 vs B10.

One team encounter contains exactly 10 individual matches.

## POINT SYSTEM

- Win = 1 point.
- Draw = 0.5 points for each team.
- Loss = 0 points.

Example:

Team A:
- 6 Wins.
- 1 Draw.
- 3 Losses.

Team B:
- 3 Wins.
- 1 Draw.
- 6 Losses.

Team A = 6.5 points.

Team B = 3.5 points.

Automatically calculate aggregate team points after verified individual match results.

Do not count pending or unverified scores.

Individual player statistics must remain separate from team aggregate points.

