# 14. DYNAMIC KNOCKOUT TOURNAMENT BRACKET
==================================================

THIS IS A CRITICAL FEATURE.

Use the tournament bracket reference image supplied by the user as the visual blueprint.

Recreate its symmetrical left-right structure.

Do not replace the requested bracket with a generic vertical list.

## BRACKET DESIGN

The bracket must contain:

- Opening Round.
- Quarter Final.
- Semi Final.
- Final.
- Champion.

For a 16-team tournament:

ROUND OF 16:
8 Matches.

QUARTER FINAL:
4 Matches.

SEMI FINAL:
2 Matches.

FINAL:
1 Match.

CHAMPION:
1 Winner.

## VISUAL LAYOUT

- Teams enter from both outer sides.
- Opening matches appear at the left and right edges.
- Winners connect to the next round.
- Quarter Finals move closer to the center.
- Semi Finals move closer to the center.
- Final appears in the middle.
- Champion appears prominently after the final.

Use:
- Horizontal connectors.
- Vertical round connectors.
- Team Logos.
- Team Names.
- Match Scores.
- Match Status.
- Winner Highlighting.
- Round Titles.
- Center Final Card.
- Champion Card.

The overall layout must closely match the uploaded reference image.

## DYNAMIC PARTICIPANT SUPPORT

Support:

- 4 Participants.
- 8 Participants.
- 16 Participants.
- 32 Participants.
- 64 Participants.
- 128 Participants.
- Any larger supported participant count.

Calculate bracket size automatically using the next suitable power of two.

Examples:

10 participants:
16-slot bracket with 6 BYEs.

24 participants:
32-slot bracket with 8 BYEs.

50 participants:
64-slot bracket with 14 BYEs.

BYE RULES:

- Automatically advance eligible participants.
- Never create fake matches for BYEs.
- Never create fake scores.
- Keep the bracket structurally correct.

## BRACKET INTERACTION

Users can:

- View all tournament rounds.
- View match details.
- View public scores.
- View team profiles.
- View participant information.
- Follow tournament progress.

Management can:

- Arrange seeding.
- Randomize draws.
- Assign first-round matchups.
- Change future match schedules.
- Verify results.
- Correct results with audit logs.
- Manage withdrawals.
- Manage disqualifications.
- Manage BYEs.

## AUTOMATIC BRACKET PROGRESSION

Only verified match winners advance.

Each winner must advance to exactly one correct next-round position.

Prevent:

- Duplicate participants.
- Duplicate matches.
- Invalid progression.
- Pending matches advancing.
- Incorrect bracket positions.
- Reprocessing the same completed match.

Tournament completion requires a verified final result.

==================================================
# 15. TEAM KNOCKOUT RULES
==================================================

In BID Team Tournaments, the knockout bracket represents Team vs Team encounters.

Each encounter contains 10 individual player matches.

The team with the higher aggregate points advances.

If both teams have equal points, use the configured tournament tie-breaker.

Supported tie-breakers:

- Extra Decider Match.
- Goal Difference.
- Management-approved Replay.

Never randomly choose a winner.

Only verified team results can advance.

==================================================
# 16. SOLO KNOCKOUT RULES
==================================================

In Solo Tournaments:

- Every bracket match represents one player versus another.
- Winner advances.
- Loser is eliminated.
- BYEs are handled automatically.
- Use the same symmetrical bracket design.

